{"id":"s2.1.3","slug":"powers-of-2-3-5","title":"Powers of 2, 3, 5","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Memorizing powers of 2, 3, and 5 is beneficial for a variety of problems, from approximations to logarithms. While some higher powers can be calculated from known squares (e.g., $7^4 = (7^2)^2 = 49^2$), the following powers are useful to have memorized for quick recall:</p><div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-4 text-sm\"><div><strong>2³</strong> = 8</div><div><strong>3³</strong> = 27</div><div><strong>5³</strong> = 125</div><div><strong>2⁴</strong> = 16</div><div><strong>3⁴</strong> = 81</div><div><strong>5⁴</strong> = 625</div><div><strong>2⁵</strong> = 32</div><div><strong>3⁵</strong> = 243</div><div><strong>5⁵</strong> = 3125</div><div><strong>2⁶</strong> = 64</div><div><strong>3⁶</strong> = 729</div><div><strong>2⁷</strong> = 128</div><div><strong>3⁷</strong> = 2187</div><div><strong>2⁸</strong> = 256</div><div><strong>2⁹</strong> = 512</div><div><strong>2¹⁰</strong> = 1024</div></div>","summary":"Memorizing powers of 2, 3, and 5 is beneficial for a variety of problems, from approximations to logarithms.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem that requires knowing a power of 2, 3, or 5.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $5^3 + 3^3 + 2^3$.","answer":"160","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $2^3 - 3^3 - 4^3$.","answer":"-83","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $(\\sqrt{64} - \\sqrt{36})^5$.","answer":"32","kind":"exact","tags":["logs-exponents"]},{"id":4,"text":"If $5^x = 125$, what is $x^5$?","answer":"243","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $4^3 - 5^3$.","answer":"-61","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":6,"text":"If $2^{x+1} = 32$, what is $x - 1$?","answer":"3","kind":"exact","tags":["logs-exponents"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $2^3 + 3^3 + 5^3$.","answer":"160","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic"]},{"id":8,"text":"Calculate $5^3 - 3^3$.","answe